        The maze has  

* 3033 rows, numbered \(1,\dots ,3033\);  
* 3032 columns, numbered \(1,\dots ,3032\);  

In each middle row \(r\;(2\le r\le 3032)\) there is exactly one invisible gate, and no two rows contain a gate in the same column.  
Hence the set of gate positions is a one‑to‑one mapping  

\[
f:\{2,\dots ,3032\}\longrightarrow \{1,\dots ,3032\},
\qquad |{\rm Im}(f)|=3031 .
\]

Consequently there is **exactly one column** that never contains a gate; call it the *safe column* \(c^{*}\).  
If the explorer ever reaches the bottom row while staying in column \(c^{*}\) he succeeds; any other column contains a gate somewhere and will teleport him back on the first visit to that gate.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### A strategy that always works

1. Keep a list of columns that have not yet been proved unsafe.  
2. In the \(i\)-th attempt choose any column \(c_i\) from that list, start at row 1, column \(c_i\) and walk straight **down**.  

   *If the explorer reaches row 3033* – the safe column has been chosen and he exits.  

   *If he steps on a gate* (necessarily the unique gate of some row \(r\)), he is instantly teleported back to the start. He now knows the gate’s position \((r,c_i)\); therefore column \(c_i\) is unsafe and is removed from the list.

3. Repeat with the next still‑unknown column.

Because each attempt discovers at most one gate (the teleportation occurs at the first gate encountered), after \(m\) unsuccessful attempts the explorer has identified exactly \(m\) distinct unsafe columns.  
When the safe column is finally selected the explorer reaches the bottom row in that same attempt.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### Worst‑case number of attempts

There are \(3031\) unsafe columns (the columns occupied by the gates) and one safe column.  
In the worst case the adversary can place the gates so that the explorer’s first \(3031\) attempts each hit a different gate, leaving the safe column as the last column he tries.

Thus the strategy needs at most  

\[
\underbrace{3031}_{\text{discover all gates}}+ \underbrace{1}_{\text{go down the safe column}}
= 3032
\]

attempts.

