        \[
f=\sum_{i=1}^{2025}a_i^{2}-\sum_{i=1}^{2023}a_i a_{i+2},
\qquad 
1=a_1\le a_2\le\cdots\le a_{2025}=199 .
\]

---

### 1.  Re‑write \(f\)

\[
\begin{aligned}
a_i^{2}-a_i a_{i+2}
&=\frac12\Big[(a_i-a_{i+2})^{2}+a_i^{2}-a_{i+2}^{2}\Big] .
\end{aligned}
\]

Summing for \(i=1,\dots ,2023\) gives  

\[
\sum_{i=1}^{2023}\!\bigl(a_i^{2}-a_i a_{i+2}\bigr)
=\frac12\sum_{i=1}^{2023}(a_i-a_{i+2})^{2}
+\frac12\bigl(a_1^{2}+a_2^{2}-a_{2024}^{2}-a_{2025}^{2}\bigr).
\]

Hence  

\[
\boxed{\,f=
\frac12\sum_{i=1}^{2023}(a_i-a_{i+2})^{2}
+\frac12\bigl(1+a_2^{2}+a_{2024}^{2}+199^{2}\bigr)\,}.
\tag{1}
\]

All terms are non‑negative.

---

### 2.  Split into odd and even subsequences  

Put  

\[
b_j=a_{2j-1}\;(j=1,\dots ,1013),\qquad 
c_j=a_{2j}\;(j=1,\dots ,1012).
\]

Both sequences are non‑decreasing integers,
\[
b_1=1,\;b_{1013}=199,\qquad 
b_j\le c_j\le b_{j+1}\;(1\le j\le1012).
\]

Define the gaps  

\[
d_j=b_{j+1}-b_j\in\{0,1\},\qquad 
e_j=c_{j+1}-c_j\ge0 .
\]

Because \(\sum_{j=1}^{1012}d_j=b_{1013}-b_1=198\).

From the relation \(c_j\in[b_j,b_{j+1}]\) we have  

\[
e_j=d_j+x_{j+1}-x_j,
\qquad
x_j=
\begin{cases}
0,&c_j=b_j,\\
1,&c_j=b_{j+1}=b_j+1,
\end{cases}
\]
and \(x_j=0\) whenever \(d_j=0\).

Consequently  

\[
\sum_{j=1}^{1012}d_j^{2}=198,\qquad
\sum_{j=1}^{1011}e_j^{2}\ge\sum_{j=1}^{1011}e_j .
\tag{2}
\]

The total increase of the even subsequence is  

\[
c_{1012}-c_1=\sum_{j=1}^{1011}e_j
= \sum_{j=1}^{1012}d_j - d_{1012}+x_{1012}-x_1
=197+x_{1012}-x_1 .
\]

Since \(x_{1012},x_1\in\{0,1\}\) and \(d_{1012}=1\) is allowed,
the smallest possible increase is \(197\) (take \(x_{1012}=x_1=0\)).
Thus the right‑hand side of (2) is at least \(197\), and it is attained
by choosing  

* all \(d_j=0\) except for the last \(198\) gaps, where \(d_j=1\);
* \(x_j=0\) for every \(j\) (i.e. \(c_j=b_j\)).

With this choice  

\[
\sum_{j=1}^{1012}d_j^{2}=198,\qquad
\sum_{j=1}^{1011}e_j^{2}=197,\qquad
a_2=c_1=1,\qquad a_{2024}=c_{1012}=b_{1012}=198 .
\]

---

### 3.  Minimal value of \(f\)

Insert these numbers into (1):

\[
\begin{aligned}
f_{\min}
&=\frac12\bigl(198+197\bigr)
   +\frac12\bigl(1+1^{2}+198^{2}+199^{2}\bigr)\\[2mm]
&=\frac12\cdot395+\frac12\cdot78807\\[2mm]
&=197.5+39403.5\\[2mm]
&=39601 .
\end{aligned}
\]

Because each step above uses a proven lower bound, this value cannot be
improved.  

