One extremal set (barycentric labels): [(4, 0, 0), (3, 0, 1), (2, 0, 2),
                                        (1, 0, 3), (0, 0, 4), (0, 1, 3), (0, 2, 2)]
Required n = 8
```

The extremal 7‑point set consists of the five points on the left side of the
triangle together with the two points just above the bottom‑left corner.
No three of these points form an isosceles triangle, and any addition of a
further point forces an isosceles triple.

Hence the smallest integer \(n\) with the required property is **8**.

