Since the inequality reduces to  

\[
\bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{6} y_i\bigr)^{\!3}\;\ge\;C\,
\sum_{i=1}^{6}\gcd(y_i,y_{i+1})\,
\operatorname{lcm}(y_{i+1},y_{i+2}),
\]

the largest constant \(C\) that works for **all** admissible 6‑tuples is exactly the minimum of the ratio, i.e.

\[
\boxed{C = 36}.
\]

Thus for any positive integers \(x_1,\dots ,x_6\),

\[
\bigl(x_1+\dots +x_6\bigr)^{\!3}\;\ge\;36\,
\gcd(x_1,\dots ,x_6)\,
\sum_{i=1}^{6}\gcd(x_i,x_{i+1})\,
\operatorname{lcm}(x_{i+1},x_{i+2}),
\]

and the constant \(36\) cannot be increased.

