For the terms to be integers we must have  

\[
k\mid a_{k-1}\qquad\text{for every }k\ge 1 .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Eliminate the division

Multiply the recurrence by \(k!\):

\[
k!\,a_{k}= (k-1)!\,a_{k-1}+k!\,k^{\,n-1}.
\]

Define  

\[
b_{k}=k!\,a_{k}\;(k\ge 0),\qquad b_{0}=a .
\]

Then  

\[
b_{k}=b_{k-1}+k!\,k^{\,n-1}\qquad(k\ge 1),
\]

hence  

\[
b_{k}=a+\sum_{i=1}^{k} i!\,i^{\,n-1}.
\]

Consequently  

\[
a_{k}= \frac{a+\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{k} i!\,i^{\,n-1}}{k!}.
\]

