\[
S_{m}= \sum_{i=1}^{m} i!\,i^{\,n-1}.
\]

Then  

\[
S_{m}=S_{m-1}+m!\,m^{\,n-1},
\]

so  

\[
S_{m}\equiv S_{m-1}\pmod{m!}.
\]

Consequently the right‑hand sides of (4) for successive values of \(m\) are
