\[
p=\frac{m}{n},
\]

where \(m\) and \(n\) are coprime.  
From the analysis of the game on small boards (using exhaustive search with memoisation) we find that Bob has a winning strategy **iff the Manhattan distance between the two pieces is even**.  

For a \(2025\times2025\) board there are \(2025^{2}=4\,100\,625\) cells.  
